Admit a known-unicast Wi-Fi/QinQ pair in one VLAN-unaware bridge.

Require current FDB ownership, live forwarding ports and ordinary Ethernet
hierarchies. Preserve host fallback for customer VLAN bridging, hairpin,
isolation/locked-port policy and same-switch LAN forwarding. FDB misses and
temporarily blocked ports are retryable. Existing ECM move/delete handlers
and QinQ topology invalidation retire stale rules. Routed paths are unchanged.
Requires the RCU bridge-port-state helper in the kernel patch set.

